20. Security and Workspace Membership

REST endpoint security: GET /workspaces/{workspaceId}/presence requires a valid JWT. The existing anyRequest().authenticated() in SecurityConfig covers this — no additional requestMatchers are needed.

WebSocket/event security: Presence events are broadcast to /topic/workspace/{workspaceId}/presence via SimpMessagingTemplate. The SimpleBroker only delivers messages to sessions that have subscribed to that topic. Since STOMP subscriptions require a prior authenticated CONNECT, only authenticated users receive presence events.

Workspace membership check: The prototype does not enforce workspace membership in AreaService (documented known limitation). The presence endpoint will follow the same approach — authenticate the caller, use the prototype workspace ID from PrototypeProperties, and not check workspace membership explicitly. If the workspaceId in the path does not match the prototype workspace ID, return an empty list (presence state only exists for the prototype workspace). No 404 for unknown workspace (consistent with the existing prototype workspace handling pattern, though checking can be added if desired).

Not exposed: session IDs, JWT contents, email addresses.

