27. Known Limitations

- Presence state is cleared on backend restart (ephemeral in-process)
- Multi-instance deployments cannot share presence without Redis (documented as future work)
- Heartbeat timeout delay (~10 s default) means a user may appear active briefly after abnormal disconnect
- If a user's JWT expires while connected, their WebSocket session may remain active until the next reconnect cycle; the Task 16 reconnect will eventually detect the expiry and call deactivate(), at which point SessionDisconnectEvent fires and presence is cleaned up

